  {
   "id": "dtkdcTEGEQAJ",
   "from": "Lorenzo Crippa",
   "author": "de9071e8091a07a9",
   "date": "2019-07-29T10:55:12Z",
   "subject": "Re: plot all sample lines in an ecdf, but color by treatment",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Dear Ben,<div><br></div><div>I think I don’t understand what your goal is. If you simply want to plot the four lines (corresponding to the four samples) coloured by treatment (thus, two will have one colour, and the other two will have a different one), you might simply type:</div><div><br></div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187)\"><code>ggplot<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>test_df<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> aes<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>x<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span>length<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> y <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">..</span>y<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">..,</span> group<font color=\"#666600\">=</font>sample<font color=\"#666600\">,</font> color<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span>treatment<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><br></code></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187)\"><code>  stat_ecdf<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>geom <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;step&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> size <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.75</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><br></code></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187)\"><code>  scale_x_continuous<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>expand <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> c<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span> name<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;Length&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><br></code></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187)\"><code>  scale_y_continuous<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>limits <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> c<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(-.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">01</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1.01</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span> expand <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> c<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span> name <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;cumulative frequency&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></code></div></div><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div>Yet, this would make it impossible to distinguish what line refers to the first vs the second and what line refers to the third vs the fourth sample.</div><div><br></div><div>Alternatively, you could differentiate the four samples by line type and the two treatments by colour:</div><div><br></div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187)\"><code>ggplot<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>test_df<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> aes<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>x<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span>length<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> y <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">..</span>y<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">..,</span> linetype<font color=\"#666600\">=</font>sample<font color=\"#666600\">,</font> color<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span>treatment<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><br></code></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187)\"><code>  stat_ecdf<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>geom <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;step&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> size <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.75</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><br></code></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187)\"><code>  scale_x_continuous<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>expand <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> c<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span> name<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;Length&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><br></code></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187)\"><code>  scale_y_continuous<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>limits <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> c<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(-.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">01</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1.01</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span> expand <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> c<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span> name <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;cumulative frequency&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></code></div><div><code><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><br></span></code></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div></div><div>This would let the viewer tell what line refers to a given sample.</div><div><br></div><div>All the best,</div><div>Lorenzo</div><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On 29 Jul 2019, at 12:01, Ben Temperton &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">btemp...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi All,<div><br></div><div>I have a large dataset where I am trying to compare the distributions between treatments using ECDF. In this toy example, I have two treatments, each with two samples. I want to plot all 4 sample ECDFs on a single plot, but colored by treatment. I can get it to color the lines by sample (giving 4 colored lines), OR I can get it to plot by treatment (giving 2 colored lines). What I can&#39;t figure out is how to plot all four lines, but color them by treatment:</div><div><br></div><div>This gives me the nearest to what I want (but with 4 colors):</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>ggplot2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br><br>test_df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">500</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> sd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span><br>                              rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">501</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> sd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span><br>                              rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">200</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> sd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span><br>                              rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">201</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> sd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span><br>                     treatment</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;treatment.1&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span> <br>                               rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;treatment.1&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span><br>                               rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;treatment.2&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span><br>                               rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;treatment.2&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span><br>                     sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;sample.1&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span> <br>                              rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;sample.2&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span><br>                              rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;sample.3&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span><br>                              rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;sample.4&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span><br><br><br>ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>test_df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">..</span><span>y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">..,</span><span> color</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span><br>  stat_ecdf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>geom </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;step&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> size </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.75</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span><br>  scale_x_continuous</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>expand </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span> name</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Length&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span><br>  scale_y_continuous</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>limits </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(-.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">01</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.01</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span> expand </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span> name </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;cumulative frequency&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">How do I get all four lines to plot, but colored by treatment?</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Thanks!</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Ben</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
